 "notes": "Overall: 35 stations, numbered 81–114 plus 109B (Ailsa Craig). No keepers are named in this list; the note says their names are under \"Diary from the Stations\" (starting at line 4023). No light characters are given, and no type (L.H./L.V.) is printed for any row.\n\nHow I filled the fields:\n- Fragments: I copied each line as printed, inside spacing included, but dropped the indentation at the start of the line.\n- Other: this holds \"returns in 6 years; value (Roman); height in feet\", with the parts joined by \"; \".\n- Marks: \"*\" means returns were sent in 1885.\n- Names and places: names keep the comma printed after them. A locality after the name is put in place, without its trailing comma.\n\nSub-headings: only two are printed, \"Sutherland\" (81–82) and \"Outer Hebrides\" (83 onward). Every row after Butt of Lewis is printed under \"Outer Hebrides\", even though most of those stations are not in the Outer Hebrides: Skye, Mull, Islay, Kintyre, Clyde and Galloway. I kept the heading as printed. Any further sub-headings the original had may have been lost in the transcription. The section itself is WEST COAST OF SCOTLAND.\n\nRows to check:\n- Stornoway (84), \"2 lights\": a brace joins two values, II. and I., with one height, 56. I put \"2 lights,\" and both values in other and the brace in marks.\n- Monach Isles (86): a brace joins two lights, I. at 150 ft and II. at 62 ft.\n- Skerryvore and Hynish Signal Tower (93): the row wraps onto line 3998.\n- Ailsa Craig (109B): no returns count, value or height. \"1885,\" probably means the station was added in 1885; I put it in other.\n- Ardnamurchan (92) has a value (I.) but no height.\n- Sanda (105) has only the returns count (0), with no value or height.\n\nPossible inconsistencies, kept as printed:\n- Rona (89) has 0 returns in 6 years but is starred for 1885. That doesn't add up, unless the 6-year column leaves out 1885 or one of the two is a misprint.\n- \"Kyleakin, W, Ross,\" uses a comma after W where \"W.\" (Wester Ross) is presumably meant.\n\nSpellings kept as printed, with the usual modern forms:\n- Island Ghlais = Eilean Glas\n- Rhu Stoir = Rhu Stoer\n- Dhuheartach = Dubh Artach\n- Lochindaul = Loch Indaal\n- Devaar = Davaar\n- Skervuile = Skervuile/Skervuile Rock\n- Rhuvaal = Rhuvaal (Islay)\n- M'Arthur's Head = McArthur's Head",
